<title>USA: KU, LG&amp;E file Va. merger application.</title>
<headline>KU, LG&amp;E file Va. merger application.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1997-07-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>KU Energy Corp said it and LG&amp;E Energy Corp jointly filed on Friday an application with the Virginia State Corporation Commission seeking authorization to merge the two companies.</p>
<p>KU Energy operates in Virginia as Old Dominion Power, which serves 29,000 customers in five southwest Virginia counties. In 1996, it had annual revenues of $41 million.</p>
<p>LG&amp;E Energy and KU Energy announced on May 21 that each company's board of directors unanimously approved the merger agreement.</p>
</text>
